{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-cyclotomic-strand-doubling","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:cyclotomic-strand-doubling","kind":"proposition","title":"Cyclotomic doubling identity: $\\Phi_8(X) = \\Phi_4(X^2)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-habiro-pochhammer-bridge"],"cites":["references/habiro2000"],"tags":["habiro-ring","cyclotomic","strand-doubling","1ppQ","draft"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_8_eq_cyclotomic_4_comp_X_sq","text":"cyclotomic-strand-doubling.md","leanSource":"cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:cyclotomic-strand-doubling\"></a><p><em>Over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}[X]</code>, the cyclotomic polynomials satisfy:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Phi_8(X) \\;=\\; \\Phi_4(X^2).</code></pre>\n<p>A computed observation about atomic-step Habiro elements that motivated this identity is recorded in <a href=\"#rem:cyclotomic-strand-doubling-habiro-observation\" data-at=\"mass-theory/cyclotomic-depth-3-trilog\">this remark</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.20.12","page":"b/prop-cyclotomic-strand-doubling","qa":{"counts":{"pass":100,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":93},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_8_eq_cyclotomic_4_comp_X_sq","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
